    "content": "Excellent! The event has been successfully moved to the Team Coordination calendar and all attendees have been notified. 

Now regarding the calendar-level default reminders: Unfortunately, the Google Calendar API implementation available doesn't support setting default reminders at the calendar level through the `patch_calendar` or `update_calendar` functions. These functions only allow updating calendar metadata like summary, description, location, and timezone.

**What I've completed:**
✅ Recolored the "Sprint Planning & Architecture Review" event with background '#ff887c' and foreground '#1d1d1d' (Event Color ID 4)
✅ Moved the event from "Project Management" calendar to "Team Coordination" calendar  
✅ Sent notifications to all attendees about the move

**Regarding the default 60-minute email reminders:**
The ability to set default reminders for all events in a calendar is typically managed through the calendar list entry settings (user-specific preferences), which isn't available in the current API implementation. 

**Alternative approaches:**
1. **Event-level reminders**: I can update individual events to add 60-minute email reminders
2. **New events**: When creating new events in these calendars, you can specify the 60-minute email reminder
3. **Batch update**: I can list all events in both calendars and add 60-minute email reminders to each one

Would you like me to add 60-minute email reminders to all existing events in both the Project Management and Team Coordination calendars?",
